---
import PageShell from '../components/PageShell.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
---
<PageShell ogImage="/og/p-resources.png"
  title="Free spreadsheet templates for marketplace sellers"
  description="Working Excel templates for reimbursement claims, settlement reconciliation and SKU-level profit tracking. No email required."
  eyebrow="Free templates"
  h1="Spreadsheets that do the boring part"
  lede="No signup, no email step, no download gate — the file is a direct link. Type in the blue cells and the rest calculates."
  crumb={{ label: 'Resources', href: '/resources/' }}
  rail={[{href:'/quiz/',label:'Which model fits you'},{href:'/costs/',label:'What it costs to start'},{href:'/guides/',label:'All guides'}]}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>FBA Reimbursement &amp; Claim Tracker</h2>
    <p>
      Amazon does not auto-credit everything it owes you. This tracks what you have found, what you have
      filed, what came back and what is still open, so claims stop falling through the follow-up window.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Sheet</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Dashboard</td><td>Total owed, total recovered, recovery rate, claims to follow up</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Claim Tracker</td><td>One row per claim — date found, case ID, type, ASIN, units, value, status</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Claim Types Guide</td><td>Common claim categories and where to check for each</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Settings</td><td>Follow-up window and status rules</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <a class="btn" href="/downloads/fba-reimbursement-claim-tracker.xlsx" download><span>Download the .xlsx</span><span class="arw" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a>
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Excel or Google Sheets. Type in the blue cells; the rest calculates. Nothing is tracked and no
      email is collected — the link above is the file.
    </p>

    <h2>How to use it without wasting a week</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Start with one claim category rather than auditing everything at once.</li>
      <li>Log the claim the day you find it, not the day you file it — the date-found column is what makes the follow-up window work.</li>
      <li>Record estimated value even when you are unsure. An approximate figure you can correct beats an empty cell.</li>
      <li>Review open claims weekly. Most of the money lost in reimbursements is lost to claims nobody chased.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The reimbursement rules, eligibility and claim windows are set by Amazon and change. Check the
      current requirements in Seller Central before filing — this template organises your work, it does
      not tell you what qualifies.
    </p>

    <h2>Other trackers</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Disclosure:</strong> extended editions of this tracker, a payout and settlement
      reconciliation workbook, and a SKU-level profit tracker are sold by this site's publisher through a
      separate Etsy shop. We have a direct commercial interest in those products. The version above is
      complete and free, and nothing on this site is scored, ranked or recommended on the basis of that
      interest. We mention it once here rather than putting a buy button on every page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Faq items={[
    { q: 'Do I need to give an email address?', a: 'No. The download is a direct link to the file. There is no form, no list and no follow-up sequence.' },
    { q: 'Will it work in Google Sheets?', a: 'Yes. Upload the .xlsx to Drive and open it with Sheets. Some conditional formatting may render slightly differently, but the calculations carry over.' },
    { q: 'Does the template tell me what Amazon owes me?', a: 'No. It organises and tracks claims you identify. Eligibility rules and claim windows are set by Amazon and change — check current requirements in Seller Central.' },
    { q: 'Can I use it for a client or my own business?', a: 'Yes, for your own or your clients\' operations. Redistributing or reselling the file is not permitted.' },
  ]} />
</PageShell>
